/target
.DS_Store

# ── Beads stays on this machine ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The issue database is not published with the code, by decision (maintainer,
# 2026-10-22). The Dolt database under .beads/ holds every bead body and close
# reason written while building this, and those quote measured failures from
# private clusters, upstream bead identifiers and internal hostnames. None of
# that is secret, and none of it is anybody else's to receive either.
#
# bd's own .beads/.gitignore already excludes the database and the JSONL
# backup, leaving config.yaml and metadata.json tracked. The whole directory is
# excluded here instead, so the decision does not depend on a vendored ignore
# file staying as it is.
/.beads/
*.gate.lock*

# Everything else bd generates, for the same reason plus one more: the
# SessionStart hook in .claude/settings.json runs `bd prime`, so committing it
# would hand a fresh clone a hook that invokes a tool the cloner may not have.
# `.claude/skills/` is NOT ignored -- those are the project's conventions and
# REUSE.toml accounts for them.
/.agents/
/.codex/
/.cursor/
/AGENTS.md
/.claude/settings.json
